KG42.register("source_edge_archive-86ef023b5c09aa855ec037cf",{"id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R016::E::v141-c-R016-E001","paper":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding","rule_id":"v141-c-R016","rule_ref":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R016","record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R016-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward"]},"evidence_class":"S","provenance_gate":"direct_C_edge_with_constraint_and_source_excerpt","scientific_acceptance":false,"accepted_constraint_ids":["v141-c-R016-C001"],"held_constraint_ids":[],"semantic_review_status":"supported","source":"COMP-58e2723fe0b22957","target":"COMP-7463d1518c82517a","source_occurrence_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R016::V::clearing.local","target_occurrence_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-c-R016::V::settlement.payment","source_unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M03-ancillary-service::clearing.local","target_unit_id":"25-p2p_ancillary_bidding::v141-a-M03-ancillary-service::settlement.payment","omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. | Monetary adjustments to existing P2P energy trading agreements for Type-1 ancillary-service provision. | Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. | Table 1 compensation arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. | Table 1 penalty arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. | Type-1 ancillary-service demand reduction originally supplied under P2G residual-balancing agreements.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]},"active":true,"source_signature":"1b55302186c72f94dc4bf255f8c58837106855fbaf07e17209fb3b8690ef87f2","relation_scope":"original_occurrence_pair_only","internal_to_parent":false,"source_science":{"mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03-ancillary-service","source_definition":"The utility, acting as coordinator of the community's ancillary-service procurement, determines which bids are accepted and the quantities procured. Scope: The utility's coordination of ancillary-service procurement from customers in the P2P energy trading community during the ancillary-service Agreement Period. Condition: After collecting customers' ancillary-service bids. Procurement quotas should initially distribute the requested service equally among submitting customers; quotas exceeding customers' bids are redistributed to customers needing additional quotas. Scope: Ancillary-service quota allocation among submitting customers in the P2P energy trading community, separately for each target time slot. Condition: After collecting ancillary-service bids, during quota distribution. Set the customer's final procurement quota equal to its submitted ancillary-service bid. Scope: Step III of ancillary-service procurement allocation, for each submitting customer and target time slot. Condition: The customer's distributed quota is at least its submitted ancillary-service bid. The customer chooses its final procurement quota between zero and its distributed quota, inclusive. Scope: Step III of ancillary-service procurement allocation, for each submitting customer and target time slot. Condition: The customer's distributed quota is below its submitted ancillary-service bid.","target_definition":"The allocated service quantity is used to calculate the customer's reward from the utility: Equation (23) multiplies the procured quantity by the ancillary-service price. Scope: Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. Condition: A Type-1 ancillary-service quantity is procured from a customer through the community procurement-allocation procedure. Prices specified in the affected P2P agreements enter the monetary adjustments. Compensation uses each agreement's price minus the feed-in tariff, multiplied by its reduced demand component and time-slot duration; the electricity payment avoided for that component uses the agreement's full price. Scope: Monetary adjustments to existing P2P energy trading agreements for Type-1 ancillary-service provision. Condition: The customer's baseline net load is positive, and Type-1 service reduces demand originally supplied through P2P agreements. The additional generated electricity is purchased by the utility at the feed-in tariff rate. Scope: Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. Condition: More electricity is generated in the ancillary-service adjustment. The additional consumed electricity is supplied by the utility at its retail price. Scope: Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. Condition: More electricity is consumed in the ancillary-service adjustment. An extra payment is owed to compensate the relevant customers for their revenue loss. Scope: Table 1 compensation arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. Condition: The ancillary-service adjustment violates a P2P energy trading agreement. No penalty is payable for the P2G agreement violation in these adjustment cases. Scope: Table 1 penalty arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. Condition: The ancillary-service adjustment violates a P2G residual-balancing agreement. The customer owes no P2G breach penalty and no longer owes the electricity charge for the demand that has been reduced. Scope: Type-1 ancillary-service demand reduction originally supplied under P2G residual-balancing agreements. Condition: The customer's baseline net load is positive, and the reduced demand was originally supplied by the utility.","constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The allocated service quantity is used to calculate the customer's reward from the utility: Equation (23) multiplies the procured quantity by the ancillary-service price. Scope: Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. Condition: A Type-1 ancillary-service quantity is procured from a customer through the community procurement-allocation procedure.","expression":"\\Delta B^{AS}_{q_{i,t}} = p_t^{AS}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T.","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R016-x-q-it"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-theta-pAS-t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward"]}],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p06-c2r1__v141-a-M03-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Applied Energy 278 (2020) 115671 ng After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"After collecting the bids from the customers in the P2P energy trading community (a time window can be defined in the Agreement Period for this purpose), the power utility needs to decide which of and to what extent the bids are to be accepted/declined. To achieve the fairness, the power utility in principle should distribute the amount of services to be procured averagely on the customers who have submitted the bids. However, the amount of services to be procured from each customer (called as the 'quota') calculated in this way may be higher than some customers' bids, and thus the surplus quotas can be given to other customers in need. With the above considerations, the process detailed in Fig. 3 is proposed for the power utility to decide the amount of services to be procured from the customers."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","location":{"location_id":"src-212077b9a1-p07-c1r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Without loss of generality, it is assumed that the magnitude of Type-1 AS procured from a customer i","equation_id":"(23)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Without loss of generality, it is assumed that the magnitude of Type-1 AS procured from a customer i for the time slot t is \\(q_{i,t}\\) (kW), as decided through the procedure shown in Fig. 3. Recall that the Type-1 AS refers to the demand reduction or generation increase of the customer i as a whole, which is measured with the baseline being the net load profile of the customer, \\(NL^*_{i,t}\\), calculated in Section 3.2. First of all, because of the provision of the ancillary service, the customer will receive reward from the power utility, as presented in Section 5.1.2. The associated benefit, \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{AS}\\), is expressed as \\(\\Delta B_{q_{i,t}}^{AS}=p_t^{AS}\\cdot q_{i,t}\\quad \\forall i\\in I^*, t\\in T.\\) (23)"}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM_DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Forward ancillary-service procurement among customers in the P2P community, for each target-period time slot. | Monetary adjustments to existing P2P energy trading agreements for Type-1 ancillary-service provision. | Table 1 arrangements balancing electricity changes caused by ancillary-service provision. | Table 1 compensation arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. | Table 1 penalty arrangements for ancillary-service changes involving more electricity generated or consumed. | Type-1 ancillary-service demand reduction originally supplied under P2G residual-balancing agreements.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E14-table1-adjustments","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward","v141-b-g02-E20-eq30-p2g-reduction-benefit","v141-b-g02-E22-eq32-penalty-cost","v141-b-g02-E23-eq33-avoided-p2p-cost-benefit"]},"source_record":{"edge_id":"v141-c-R016-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R016-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E11-as-step3-fairness","v141-b-g02-E15-eq23-as-reward"]},"paper_scope_note":"CDA, ancillary services, and residual agreement adjustment are kept separate; arrival events, matched orders, and the next ZIP update are not variables at the same time point; reward and compensation costs are different settlement sub-items."}});
